---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="dark">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
  <meta name="description" content="Portfolio of Sambeet Sekhar Panda, a backend-focused software engineer building scalable APIs, data systems, developer infrastructure, cloud platforms, and AI-enabled workflows." />
  <meta property="og:title" content="Sambeet Sekhar Panda — Backend-Focused Software Engineer" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="Backend engineering, Go, Python, APIs, distributed systems, databases, cloud infrastructure, developer tooling, and applied AI." />
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://sambeetpanda507.github.io" />
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://sambeetpanda507.github.io" />
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" />
  <title>Sambeet Sekhar Panda — Backend-Focused Software Engineer</title>
  <script is:inline>
    const t = localStorage.getItem('theme');
    document.documentElement.dataset.theme = t || (matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: light)').matches ? 'light' : 'dark');
  </script>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <nav class="wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="#top">Sambeet<span>.</span></a>
    <div class="navlinks">
      <a href="#about">About</a>
      <a href="#experience">Experience</a>
      <a href="#projects">Projects</a>
      <a href="#skills">Skills</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </div>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="icon" href="https://github.com/sambeetpanda507" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" aria-label="GitHub">GH</a>
      <a class="icon linkedin-icon" href={linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" aria-label="LinkedIn">in</a>
      <button class="icon" id="theme" aria-label="Toggle theme">◐</button>
    </div>
  </nav>
</header>

<main id="top">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div>
      <div class="status"><i></i> Building reliable backend systems & developer platforms</div>
      <p class="eyebrow">BACKEND-FOCUSED SOFTWARE ENGINEER · FULL-STACK DEVELOPER</p>
      <h1>Sambeet Sekhar <span>Panda.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">I build production-grade backend systems, APIs, data platforms, developer tooling, and AI-powered workflows — with a focus on reliability, clarity, and scalable architecture.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="primary" href="#projects">View projects ↗</a>
        <a class="secondary" href="https://github.com/sambeetpanda507" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>
        <a class="secondary" href={linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact me →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="terminal">
      <div class="dots">● ● ● <small>sambeet@portfolio ~</small></div>
      <pre><b>$</b> whoami
<strong>backend-focused software engineer</strong>

<b>$</b> primary --languages
<strong>Go        Python</strong>

<b>$</b> focus --current
<span>APIs      databases
systems   developer tooling</span>

<b>$</b> principle
<strong>clarity &gt; cleverness</strong>

<b>$</b> <em>▋</em></pre>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="about">
    <div class="label"><span>01</span> ABOUT</div>
    <div class="twocol">
      <h2>I build systems that stay <span>understandable as they grow.</span></h2>
      <div>
        <p>Backend-focused software engineer working across APIs, data systems, databases, distributed workflows, developer infrastructure, and cloud delivery.</p>
        <p>I also build AI/LLM capabilities where they solve a real product or engineering problem — from document pipelines and RAG to agent-based developer tooling.</p>
        <p>I care about clear boundaries, predictable failure modes, useful automation, and choosing the simplest architecture that can reliably carry the load.</p>
        <div class="focus">
          <b>Currently exploring</b>
          <div>{['Go Concurrency','Advanced PostgreSQL','Distributed Systems','System Design','Backend Performance','AI Agents','RAG Architecture'].map(x => <span>{x}</span>)}</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="experience">
    <div class="label"><span>02</span> EXPERIENCE & EDUCATION</div>
    <div class="timeline-stack">
      <article class="experience">
        <div><p>CURRENT</p><h3>Lead Developer</h3><strong>Starweaver</strong></div>
        <div>
          <p>Leading software engineering across backend services, system integrations, developer workflows, production delivery, and selected AI-enabled capabilities.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Design and review production APIs, backend workflows, and system integrations.</li>
            <li>Drive CI/CD, pull-request quality, release practices, and engineering automation.</li>
            <li>Build backend-heavy product capabilities, data workflows, and AI-assisted features where appropriate.</li>
            <li>Support engineers through architecture decisions, code review, and delivery planning.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="education-card">
        <div><p>2014 — 2018</p><h3>Biju Patnaik University of Technology, Odisha</h3></div>
        <div><span>Education</span><p>Undergraduate education listed on my public LinkedIn profile.</p></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="projects">
    <div class="label"><span>03</span> SELECTED WORK</div>
    <div class="heading">
      <h2>Systems, platforms, <span>and useful automation.</span></h2>
      <p>Representative work across backend architecture, databases, developer tooling, production platforms, search, and applied AI.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      {projects.map((p, i) =>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="num">0{i + 1}</div>
          <p class="tag">{p.tag}</p>
          <h3>{p.title}</h3>
          <p>{p.desc}</p>
          <div class="architecture"><b>ARCHITECTURE / STACK</b>{p.stack}</div>
          {p.source && <a class="source-link" href={linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">From public LinkedIn activity ↗</a>}
        </article>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="skills">
    <div class="label"><span>04</span> ENGINEERING TOOLKIT</div>
    <div class="skills-intro">
      <div><h2>Backend first. <span>Go & Python in focus.</span></h2></div>
      <p>I work across the stack, but I’m deliberately deepening my backend engineering around Go and Python, databases, distributed systems, APIs, reliability, and the infrastructure around them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="skill-groups">
      {skillGroups.map((group, i) =>
        <article class:list={["skill-group", i === 0 && "featured-skill"]}>
          <div class="skill-head">
            <div><span class="skill-index">0{i + 1}</span><h3>{group.title}</h3></div>
            <small>{group.note}</small>
          </div>
          <div class="skill-list">
            {group.skills.map(skill =>
              <span class:list={["skill-chip", skill.featured && "skill-highlight"]}>{skill.name}{skill.featured && <b>★</b>}</span>
            )}
          </div>
        </article>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="label"><span>05</span> ENGINEERING PHILOSOPHY</div>
    <div class="principles">
      {principles.map((p, i) => <article><span>0{i + 1}</span><h3>{p[0]}</h3><p>{p[1]}</p></article>)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap profiles">
    <div class="label"><span>06</span> PROFILES</div>
    <div class="profile-layout">
      <div>
        <h2>Code, context, <span>and the work behind it.</span></h2>
        <p>GitHub is where I publish code and experiments. LinkedIn is where I share what I’m learning and the engineering ideas behind those projects.</p>
        <div class="profile-links">
          <a class="profile-link" href="https://github.com/sambeetpanda507" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><b>GitHub</b><span>@sambeetpanda507 ↗</span></a>
          <a class="profile-link" href={linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><b>LinkedIn</b><span>Sambeet Sekhar Panda ↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58733137?v=4" alt="Sambeet Sekhar Panda GitHub avatar" width="160" height="160" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap contact" id="contact">
    <div class="label"><span>07</span> CONTACT</div>
    <h2>Let's build something <span>interesting.</span></h2>
    <p>For backend/software engineering roles, collaboration, or a good systems discussion:</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="primary" href="mailto:sambeetsekharpanda10@gmail.com">Email me ↗</a>
      <a class="secondary" href="https://github.com/sambeetpanda507" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>
      <a class="secondary" href={linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="wrap">
  <span>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Sambeet Sekhar Panda</span>
  <span><a href={linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a> · Built with Astro · Hosted on GitHub Pages</span>
</footer>

<script is:inline>
  document.getElementById('theme')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const n = document.documentElement.dataset.theme === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark';
    document.documentElement.dataset.theme = n;
    localStorage.setItem('theme', n);
  });
</script>

<style>
